# curlimages/curl — krb5 / krb5-libs 1.22.2-r1 (Alpine 3.24.3 base), HIGH
#
# Fixed in 1.22.3-r0. Alpine's package index already carries the fix
# (confirmed via `apk info krb5-libs` against a fresh alpine:3.24/edge
# pull), but curlimages/curl has not been rebuilt against it: its
# `latest` and newest version tag (8.23.0) resolve to the same image
# digest, built 2026-10-28, and there is no newer tag to pin to as of
# 2026-11-16. `--ignore-unfixed` means this exception clears itself on
# the next scan once curlimages/curl republishes.
#
# All 16 IDs below are krb5 KDC/kadmind-side bugs (unauthenticated DoS,
# memory leaks, ASN.1 decoder read overruns). curlimages/curl only runs
# the `curl` client as bwx's optional HTTP fallback (include/http),
# invoked as non-root `curl_user` when the host has no curl/wget/fetch.
# It never starts krb5kdc or kadmind, so none of these code paths are
# reachable through this image's actual usage. Accepted as
# non-exploitable here; re-run the scan after each curlimages/curl
# release and drop these entries once the fixed package appears.
